ium, where patients may have to cover part of the costs for NED.\",1\r\n16340,COMPETENCIA DE NED,The competition faced by NED in providing nutritional support and the associated economic implications.,1\r\n16295,EE.UU.,EE.UU. is one of the eight countries mentioned that has limitations in data collection for epidemiological studies.,1\r\n16288,POLONIA,\"Polonia refers to Poland, a country that is included in the epidemiological study of NED. In this context, patients in Poland may be required to cover a portion of the costs associated with NED.\",1\r\n16289,SUECIA,\"Suecia, which refers to Sweden, is identified as one of the eight countries that face limitations in data collection for epidemiological studies. Additionally, it is noted that Sweden has limited data on home nutrition, highlighting challenges in gathering comprehensive nutritional information within the country.\",1\r\n16293,PROGRAMAS DE MEDICARE,\"Programas de Medicare are federal health insurance programs in the United States for individuals aged 65 and older or disabled, covering aspects of NED.\",1\r\n16294,PROGRAMAS DE MEDICAID,\"Programas de Medicaid are health insurance programs in the United States that provide coverage for low-income individuals, including aspects of NED.\",1\r\n4366,NICE,\"The National Institute for Health and Care Excellence (NICE) is an organization that provides comprehensive guidelines related to healthcare. It focuses on various aspects of medical care, including the management of specific health conditions and the improvement of patient outcomes. NICE offers directives on the care of malnourished patients, ensuring that their nutritional needs are addressed effectively. Additionally, it provides guidelines for the prevention and management of diabetic foot problems, highlighting its commitment to addressing critical health issues and enhancing the quality of care across different patient populations.\",4\r\n16296,BANS,\"BANS, which stands for the British Artificial Nutri